    "A Growing Commercial Relationship",
    "Irish trade figures reported by The Irish Times show that approximately 422,474 metric tons of alumina, valued at €119.5 million, were exported to Russia during the first six months of 2026.",
    "Russia accounted for nearly half of the refinery's exports during that period.",
    "The figures illustrate how commercial relationships can expand even as political and diplomatic relations deteriorate.",
    "For Rusal, continued access to Irish alumina helps maintain production capacity. For Ireland, the refinery supports hundreds of jobs and contributes to Europe's aluminum supply.",
    "Both sides have substantial economic incentives to preserve the arrangement.",
    "Beyond Ireland: Europe's Strategic Dependencies",
    "European sanctions legislation contains exceptions and authorization mechanisms for several strategically important industries.",
